WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.300
In this classroom, every
pupil wears a badge:

2
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:06.200
visual, auditory or kinaesthetic.

3
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.420
The visual group gets diagrams.

4
00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:10.390
The auditory group listens.

5
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.380
The kinaesthetic group
gets hands-on tasks.

6
00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.900
Same lesson, three versions.

7
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:21.580
In one survey, 93 per cent of UK teachers
believed students learn more when teaching

8
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.190
matches their style.

9
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.830
So does it work?

10
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.280
Teach a visual learner with
pictures: will they learn more?

11
00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:30.420
If not, what would help?

12
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:34.000
In this mission, you'll unpack
the idea of a learning style:

13
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.120
a person's preferred way
of taking in information.

14
00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:41.550
And you'll meet Daniel Willingham, a
cognitive psychologist who took a hard look

15
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.980
at the evidence for it.

16
00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:47.310
Your mission: decide whether teaching
to a learning style really helps.
